  "sourceAssignment": "Completion 164 Baba Has Keke exclusively owns the full chronological baba-has-keke-part1 through part4 original families. Earlier belt staging, three-word and four-word calibrations, all four undos, 32 waits, one restart and the complete successful traversal remain. Intervening unrelated level/hunt recordings retain their separate allocations. All twenty original/sidecar files stay retained.",
  "scope": "Earlier visits establish belt staging and finite clock traces. The final restart constructs a six-belt circuit around stationary HAS, using PUSH as a fourth text token. Timed BABA HAS KEKE produces Keke when Baba melts in the lower lava; KEKE HAS BABA then produces Baba on the approach tile (511, 256) when OPEN Keke removes the SHUT door. The actual correction uses two UPs plus six waits to reach dry (511, 208) with the forward HAS rule; upper lava produces Keke, which reaches the flag. Two Baba MELTs and one Keke OPEN consumption are intentional HAS replacements. Settled map pause confirms 164 completed / nine flowers.",
